Licence notice for tom_binaries

This repository holds compiled programs, not source code. Each program is
built from a package and is licensed under that package's licence, which is
in the package's LICENSE file in its source repository.

What may go in (DP-204 (c), 2026-11-12): a binary may go in when its licence
is not copyleft - BSD, MIT, Apache and the like, licences that require no
source to be published and bind nothing the binary is combined with - whether
its source repository is public or private; GPL and other copyleft binaries
stay out. A private source repository is marked "(private)" below; its licence
still applies to the binary as stated.


| Binary (tom/<platform>/)        | Package                     | Source repository                                  | Licence      |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |
| buildkit, bk, findproject, wssetup | tom_build_kit             | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_basics          | BSD 3-Clause |
| testkit, tk                     | tom_test_kit                | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_devops          | BSD 3-Clause |
| issuekit, ik                    | tom_issue_kit               | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_devops          | BSD 3-Clause |
| tom                             | tom_build_cli               | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_devops          | BSD 3-Clause |
| astgen                          | tom_ast_generator           | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_d4rt            | BSD 3-Clause |
| d4rtgen                         | tom_d4rt_generator          | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_d4rt            | BSD 3-Clause |
| dcli                            | tom_d4rt_dcli               | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_d4rt            | BSD 3-Clause |
| dclie                           | tom_dcli_exec               | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_d4rt            | BSD 3-Clause |
| reflector, reflection_analyzer  | tom_reflector               | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_reflection      | BSD 3-Clause |
| reflectiongenerator             | tom_reflection_generator    | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_reflection      | BSD 3-Clause (Dart authors, derived from reflectable) |
| tom_bs                          | tom_vscode_bridge           | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_vscode          | BSD 3-Clause |
| validate_codespecs, spec_checks | tom_specs_clitool           | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_ai_build        | BSD 3-Clause |
| tsm, tom_secrets_manager/bin/tsm | tom_secrets_tsm            | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_secrets_clients | BSD 3-Clause |
| tom_secrets_manager/bin/tom_secrets_service, tom_secrets_manager/lib/ | tom_secrets_service | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_secrets_manager | BSD 3-Clause (its native library: tom_pqc, BSD 3-Clause, over mlkem-native and mldsa-native, Apache-2.0 or ISC or MIT; texts in tom_secrets_manager/licenses/) |
| Tom Secrets Manager.app (darwin-arm64; tsm and the service inside) | tom_secrets_app | https://github.com/al-the-bear/tom_app_secrets_manager | BSD 3-Clause (third-party notices in the app: THIRD_PARTY.md) |
| marktext (launcher script)      | -                           | this repository                                    | BSD 3-Clause (below) |

Each program also contains the code of the packages it depends on (for
example tom_d4rt, MIT; the Dart runtime and pub.dev packages, each under its
own licence). Their licences are those packages' licences; a package's
dependencies are listed in its pubspec.yaml in the source repository.

sqlite_vec/ holds the loadable extension of sqlite-vec by Alex Garcia
(https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec), dual-licensed MIT or Apache-2.0; the
licence texts are in sqlite_vec/LICENSE-MIT and sqlite_vec/LICENSE-APACHE.

pdfium/<platform>/ holds PDFium as built by the pdfium-binaries project
(https://github.com/bblanchon/pdfium-binaries; PDFium itself:
https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium), the variant without V8 and XFA.
PDFium is BSD 3-Clause; the third-party code built into it (FreeType,
HarfBuzz, ICU, libjpeg-turbo, OpenJPEG, libpng, zlib, lcms2, abseil, ...) is
under permissive licences; the pdfium-binaries build scripts are MIT. The texts
travel with the library: pdfium/<platform>/LICENSE (the build scripts) and
pdfium/<platform>/licenses/ (PDFium and every third-party component). The
release, the archive's SHA-256 and the date taken in are in
pdfium/<platform>/pdfium.version.json.

